.TH "CREDENTIAL.ISCONDITIONALMEDIATIONAVAILABLE_STATIC" "3JS" "April 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Credential.isConditionalMediationAvailable_static \- Credential:
isConditionalMediationAvailable() static method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]isConditionalMediationAvailable()\f[B]\f[R] static method
of the \f[CR]Credential\f[R] interface returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R]
which resolves to \f[CR]false\f[R].
.PP
Subclasses of \f[CR]Credential\f[R] override this method if they support
conditional mediation.
See \f[CR]PublicKeyCredential.isConditionalMediationAvailable()\f[R],
for example.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
Credential.isConditionalMediationAvailable()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]Promise\f[R] which resolves to \f[CR]false\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]await\f[R] Credential.isConditionalMediationAvailable(); \f[I]// false\f[R]
.EE
